  "title": "Iqa‘ Malfuf 2/4",
  "subtitle": "(also called Laff)",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Malfuf",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Malfuf (also called Laff) is primarily used in folk and popular Arabic music. If feels short and cyclical, and often modulates to and from other 2/4 iqa‘at like Karachi and Fox. Alternatively 2 consecutive measures of Malfuf could modulate to one measure of a 4/4 iqa‘ like Baladi or Maqsum."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Malfuf 2/4 (also called Laff ) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Malfuf Iqa‘ Malfuf (also called Laff ) is primarily used in folk and popular Arabic music. If feels short and cyclical, and often modulates to and from other 2/4 iqa‘at like Karachi and Fox . Alternatively 2 consecutive measures of Malfuf could modulate to one measure of a 4/4 iqa‘ like Baladi or Maqsum . Ya Dara Duri Fina Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Amal Hayati (1965) Umm Kulthum Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Muwashah Ya Sahi al-Sabru Waha Minni Hasan al-Haffar Muwashah Ya Sahi al-Sabru Waha Minni Sheikh Hamza Shakkur Ensemble Al Kindi Tulbah (Proposition) El-Funoun Ensemble Zaghareed: Music From The Palestinian Holy Land Iqa‘ Malfuf 2/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
